10 REM CIRCLES - THE NEAL-PITTEWAY MIDPOINT INTEGRATOR
20 REM X=X-E/2*Y : Y=Y+E*X : X=X-E/2*Y, WITH E=1/16 AND EVERYTHING
30 REM SCALED BY 1024, SO THE TWO HALF STEPS DIVIDE BY 32 EXACTLY.
40 REM ONE TURN IS 2*PI/E STEPS, WHICH IS WHY S RUNS TO 104: FEWER
50 REM AND EACH RING WOULD COME OUT AN OPEN ARC.
60 REM THERE IS NO CURSOR ADDRESSING ON THIS MACHINE, SO THE POINTS GO
70 REM INTO A 21 BY 19 GRID IN THE FREE RAM BELOW LOMEM AND THE GRID IS
80 REM PRINTED ONCE, TOP DOWN. A NAME IS ONE LETTER AND AT MOST ONE
90 REM DIGIT HERE, SO V AND W ARE THE CELL A POINT LANDS IN.
100 B=768
110 FOR I=0 TO 398
120 POKE B+I,0
130 NEXT I
140 FOR K=1 TO 3
150 X=K*3072
160 Y=0
170 FOR S=1 TO 104
180 X=X-Y/32
190 Y=Y+X/16
200 X=X-Y/32
210 V=11+(Y+512*SGN(Y))/1024
220 REM A CELL IS 7 DOTS WIDE AND 8 TALL, SO A RING NEEDS 8/7 AS MANY
230 REM COLUMNS AS ROWS TO READ ROUND: 1024*7/8 IS THE 896 HERE.
240 W=20+(X+448*SGN(X))/896
250 POKE B+(V-2)*21+W-10,1
260 NEXT S
270 NEXT K
280 REM EACH CELL IS PRINTED AS IT IS DECIDED. THE DISPLAY TAKES ONE
290 REM CHARACTER PER VIDEO FIELD AND BASIC WAITS ON IT, SO THE NEXT
300 REM CELL IS WORKED OUT INSIDE THAT WAIT AND COSTS NOTHING.
310 FOR R=2 TO 20
320 TAB 10
330 FOR C=10 TO 30
340 IF PEEK(B+(R-2)*21+C-10)=1 THEN 370
350 PRINT " ";
360 GOTO 380
370 PRINT "*";
380 NEXT C
390 PRINT
400 NEXT R
410 END
